ng for 8 min. The staining solution was removed, and the cells were washed three times with PBS and observed by laser confocal microscopy. Quantitative analysis of cell polarization The experimental group was the same as the (B) same-viability group. Cells were seeded in 6-well plates. When the incubation time was reached, the cells were fixed with 4% paraformaldehyde and incubated overnight at 4 ℃ with CD86 or CD206 primary antibodies, followed by incubation for 1 h at room temperature with secondary antibodies. The staining solution was removed, and the cells were washed three times with PBS. The cells were collected, and the cell population was detected by flow cytometry. Zeta potential of COM crystal Zeta potentials of COM crystals of different sizes were examined. In this work, 3 mg of COM crystals was weighed and dispersed in 6 mL of ethyl alcohol or RPMI-1640 culture medium. The zeta potential of the samples was determined using a Zetasizer Nano ZS laser nanoparticle size analyzer. Statistical analysis Data are presented as means ± SD. The number of individual experiments is indicated in the Figures or figure legends. One-way ANOVA was used for statistical analysis by SPSS 13.0 software. In all Figures, significance was defined as follows: *P < 0.05, **P < 0.01, ***P < 0.001. P ≥ 0.05 were considered not significant.

