Cell culture THP-1 cells were cultured in RPMI-1640 medium containing 10% fetal bovine serum and 0.05 mM β-mercaptoethanol in an incubator at 37 ℃ and 5% CO 2 . The medium was changed by replenishing or partially exchanging the fluid and passaged by centrifugation.

Macrophage differentiation Experimental grouping THP-1 cells were plated at a density of 10 6  cells/mL. The experiment was divided into three groups: (a) normal control group (NC): THP-1 cells were cultured in RPMI-1640 medium without serum; (b) differentiation group: THP-1 cells were induced to Mφs by incubation in complete culture medium containing 5 ng/mL PMA for 24 h, followed by resting for 24 h [ 28 ]; and (c) blank background group: serum-free RPMI-1640 medium only. Microscopic observation of cell morphology and hematoxylin–eosin staining (HE staining) The experimental groups were the same as the (a) normal control group and (b) differentiation group. The cells were seeded in 12-well plates. After differentiation, the cells were photographed under an inverted fluorescence microscope to observe the cell morphology. After cell attachment, the original culture medium was aspirated and washed once with PBS. Each well was fixed with 1.5 mL of 4% paraformaldehyde for 15 min, stained with hematoxylin staining solution for 15 min, rinsed with water to remove excess staining solution, added with eosin staining solution to stain for 90 s, rinsed with water to remove excess staining solution, observed by an inverted fluorescence microscope, and photographed. The nucleus was blue, and the cytoplasm was pink. Immunofluorescence detection of CD68 expression The experimental groups were the same as the (a) normal control group and (b) differentiation group. After cells were seeded on slides and differentiated, the cells were fixed using 4% paraformaldehyde fixative for 15 min and then washed three times with PBS. The cells were permeabilized for 10 min and washed three times with PBS. The cells were blocked with blocking solution for 1 h and washed three times with PBS. The cells were incubated at 4 ℃ overnight after dilution of the CD68 primary antibody at the prescribed ratio and washed three times with PBS. The cells were incubated for 70 min after dilution of the secondary antibody at the prescribed proportions and washed three times with PBS. The nuclei were stained with DAPI for 5 min and washed three times with PBS. Finally, a sealing operation was performed to fix the slide containing cells. The expression of CD68 in the treated cell sheets was observed by laser confocal microscopy. The images of immunofluorescence were semiquantitatively analyzed using ImageJ software.

